  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Arithmetic sequences add a constant; geometric sequences multiply by one. Summing their terms gives series — including the surprising fact that an infinite geometric series can have a finite total.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 7.1 — Arithmetic vs geometric",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>An <strong>arithmetic</strong> sequence has a common difference \\( d \\); a <strong>geometric</strong> sequence has a common ratio \\( r \\). Their \\( n \\)th terms are \\( a_1+(n-1)d \\) and \\( a_1 r^{\\,n-1} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arithmetic sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( S_n=\\tfrac{n}{2}\\big(a_1+a_n\\big) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Geometric sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( S_n=a_1\\dfrac{1-r^{n}}{1-r} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Infinite geometric",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( S=\\dfrac{a_1}{1-r}\\ \\ (|r|&lt;1) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the 10th term of the arithmetic sequence with \\( a_1=2 \\), \\( d=3 \\).</p>\\[ a_{10}=2+(10-1)(3)=29. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the sum of \\( 8+4+2+1+\\cdots \\)</p><p>Geometric with \\( a_1=8 \\), \\( r=\\tfrac12 \\):</p>\\[ S=\\frac{8}{1-\\tfrac12}=16. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) in the expansion of \\((3-2x)^5\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\binom{5}{2}(3)^3(-2x)^2=10\\times27\\times4x^2=1080x^2\\). Coefficient: \\(1080\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
